Inclusion criteria:
1. 1)	Age ≥ 18 years;
2. 11)	Men and women* must use effective contraceptive measures during the treatment and for at least 15 months after the last dose received; (* of childbearing age);
3. 10)	Creatinine clearance ≥ 30 mL/min
4. 12)	No known risk of irinotecan toxicity
5. 13)	No Dihydropyrimidine dehydrogenase deficit (uracil blood Level <16ng/ml);
6. 14)	Patient is willing and able to comply with the protocol for the duration of the study, including treatment and scheduled visits and examinations, including follow up;
7. 15)	Patient has valid health insurance.
8. 2)	Written informed consent obtained from the patient before any study procedure;
9. 3)	ECOG performance status of 0 to 2;
10. 4)	Histopathologically confirmed colonic adenocarcinoma with synchronous or metachronous peritoneal metastasis (PM);
11. 5)	Unresectable PM defined as any of the following: -	PCI >15 -	Extended small bowell involvement -	Poor general condition contra-indication to a major abdominal surgery (eg: a complete cytoreductive surgery ), as decided by the medico-surgical team of the investigator’s site specialised in peritoneal carcinomatosis in charge of the patient.
12. 6)	A surgical exploration performed less than 4 weeks before inclusion (if not, a laparoscopic exploration must be performed);
13. 7)	Indication of first line systemic chemotherapy for advanced / metastatic colonic adenocarcinoma. Systemic chemotherapy in an adjuvant setting is allowed if completed more than 6 months before recurrence and without persistent oxaliplatin-induced neuropathy;
14. 8)	No extended intraperitoneal adherences confirmed by surgical exploration (laparoscopy or laparotomy) in at least 9 out of 13 abdominal regions;
15. 9)	Neutrophils count ≥ 1.5 x 109/L, platelet count ≥ 100 x109/L, hemoglobin ≥ 9 g/dL; Total bilirubin < 1.5 x ULN (upper limit of normal), ASAT and ALAT <3 x ULN, Alkaline phosphatase <1.5 x ULN, Serum creatinine < 1.5 x ULN;
Exclusion criteria:
1. 1)	Other cancer treated within the last 3 years, with the exception of in situ cervical carcinoma or basocellular carcinoma;
2. 9)	Clinically relevant and uncontrolled coronary heart disease, myocardial infarction within the past 12 months;
3. 19)	Known history of hypersensibility to fluorouracil, folinic acid, irinotecan, oxaliplatin, capecitabine, cetuximab, panitumumab, bevacizumab or to any of their excipients, according to the SmPCs of these products.
4. 10)	Uncontrolled arrhythmia;
5. 20)	Concomitant treatment with brivudine, sorivudine or their chemically related analogues (according to the SmPC of fluorouracile)
6. 21)	Live attenuated vaccines and for 6 months following cessation of chemotherapy (according to the SmPCs of fluorouracile and irinotecan);
7. 22)	Concomitant use with St John's Wort (according to the SmPC of irinotecan);
8. 23)	Severe renal insufficiency (creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min, according to the SmPC of capecitabine;
9. 24)	History of allergy to red meat or tick bites or positive results of tests for IgE antibodies against cetuximab (α-1-3-galactose) (according to the SmPC of cetuximab);
10. 25)	Interstitial lung disease (according to the SmPCs of cetuximab and panitumumab);
11. 26)	Pulmonary fibrosis (according to the SmPC of panitumumab);
12. 18)	QT/QTc interval longer than 450 msec for men and longer than 470 msec for women on the inclusion ECG
13. 27)	Hypersensitivity to Chinese hamster ovary (CHO) cell products (according to the SmPC of bevacizumab)
14. 28)	Pregnancy or breast-feeding period;
15. 29)	Medical, geographical, sociological, psychological or legal conditions that would not permit the patient completing the study or signing the informed consent form.
16. 11)	Uncontrolled hypertension;
17. 12)	Inflammatory bowel disease;
18. 13)	Ongoing non-healing wounds, ulcers or bone fractures;
19. 14)	Relevant proteinuria (nephrotic syndrome); arterial thromboembolisms or severe haemorrhages within 6 months before study enrolment (except a bleeding tumour before tumour resection surgery) precluding the use of anti-VEGF drug;
20. 15)	Haemorrhagic diathesis or thrombotic tendency;
21. 16)	Peripheral neuropathy oxaliplatin-related according to the Common Toxicity Criteria for Adverse Events (CTCAE) version 5.0;
22. 17)	No reversible electrolyte disorders such as hypokalemia, hypocalcemia or hypomagnesemia.
23. 2)	Rectal cancer primary (tumor <15 cm from the anal verge);
24. 30)	Appendix cancer
25. 3) Mutational status corresponding to microsatellite instability high (MSI-H) or mismatch repair deficient (dMMR)
26. 4)	Complete or partial bowel obstruction unresponsive to medical treatment;
27. 5)	Extraperitoneal polymetastatic diseases. (Only oligometastatic1 diseases are allowed for inclusion) 1. 1oligo-metastatic disease as defined up to 3 liver metastases less than 5 cm in diameter and/or up to 3 lung nodules less than 10 mm in diameter and/or ovarian metastasis of any size.
28. 6)	History of abdominal fistula, gastrointestinal perforation, intra-abdominal abscess within 6 months prior to enrolment;
29. 7)	Active gastrointestinal bleeding;
30. 8)	Severe ongoing infection;
